Assumptions, Constraints & Dependencies
Assumptions
The following conditions are assumed to be true for the successful execution of this automation test project:
1.	The application under test is feature-stable and accessible in the test environment
2.	Test data is available and can be seeded/cleaned up automatically
3.	API documentation (Swagger/OpenAPI) is provided and up-to-date
4.	Automation engineers have access to all required tools and environments
5.	Application UI locators will use data-testid attributes for reliable test automation
6.	No major UI redesigns will occur during the automation development phase
7.	CI/CD pipeline permissions and infrastructure are available
8.	The application supports modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari) as per the browser matrix
9.	Test execution can be run in parallel across multiple workers
10.	Security policies allow Playwright to execute in the test environment
Constraints
The following limitations apply to this project:
1.	Browser Coverage: Only browsers supported by the application will be tested (Chromium, Firefox, WebKit)
2.	Device Coverage: Mobile testing will be limited to emulation; no physical device testing
3.	Environment Access: Tests will run only on Dev/Staging environments; production access is not permitted
4.	Test Data: Only synthetic/anonymized test data may be used; production data is prohibited
5.	Team Availability: Automation team consists of [X] engineers allocated [Y]% to this project
6.	Timeline: Project must be completed within [Z] weeks from project kickoff
7.	Tooling: Only open-source Playwright tools; no commercial tool licenses approved
8.	Network: Tests may be affected by network latency and firewall restrictions
9.	Compliance: All tests must comply with healthcare data privacy regulations (HIPAA/GDPR)
10.	CI/CD Integration: Only GitHub Actions/GitLab CI pipelines are supported
